# skills/favbase/SKILL.md is compared byte for byte: the favbase CLI bundles it
# with LF endings, and `npx skills add InvisibleQAQ/favbase` git-clones it (the
# skills tool fetches raw bytes only for an allowlist of owners). Under
# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' default) that clone checks it out as
# CRLF, and `favbase doctor` calls the copy stale (docs/30 #4).
skills/favbase/SKILL.md text eol=lf
